<section #eh-subject | `<subject>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · eHTML `<subject>` · JATS `<subject>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `scheme` | kwarg |  | Optional classification scheme this subject belongs to (e.g. |

Produced by: canonical `<subject>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code-block #code:eh-subject-1>
<meta>
  <subject | Ecology of large mammals>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-subject-1>
<meta>
  <subject | Ecology of large mammals>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Free-form subject. Common for general-interest documents.*

<code-block #code:eh-subject-2>
<meta>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D40>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D25>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-subject-2>
<meta>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D40>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D25>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Multiple subjects from a controlled vocabulary. The scheme
identifies the classification system; the JATS exporter
generates the appropriate &lt;subj-group subj-group-type="..."&gt; wrapper.*

<section #eh-subtitle | `<subtitle>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · eHTML `<subtitle>` · JATS `<subtitle>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

*No kwargs or boolean flags.*

Produced by: canonical `<subtitle>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code-block #code:eh-subtitle-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <subtitle | A Multi-Year Field Study in Tanzania>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-subtitle-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <subtitle | A Multi-Year Field Study in Tanzania>
</meta>
</minipage>

<section #eh-title | `<title>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · eHTML `<title>` · JATS `<article-title or book-title (inside title-group inside article-meta or book-meta)>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

*No kwargs or boolean flags.*

Produced by: canonical `<title>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code-block #code:eh-title-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-title-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Inside &lt;article&gt;, &lt;title&gt; in &lt;meta&gt; becomes &lt;article-title&gt;.*

<code-block #code:eh-title-2>
<book>
  <meta>
    <title | A Comprehensive Guide>
  </meta>
</book>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-title-2>
<book>
  <meta>
    <title | A Comprehensive Guide>
  </meta>
</book>
</minipage>

*Inside &lt;book&gt;, &lt;title&gt; in &lt;meta&gt; becomes &lt;book-title&gt;.*

<code-block #code:eh-title-3>
<meta>
  <title | The role of <i type=taxonomic | Loxodonta africana> in ecosystem dynamics>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-title-3>
<meta>
  <title | The role of <i type=taxonomic | Loxodonta africana> in ecosystem dynamics>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Titles can contain inline elements. The recursive content parsing
handles nested constructs.*

<section #eh-version | `<version>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · eHTML `<version>` · JATS `<(no direct standard element; uncertain — may map to article-version or custom-meta)>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

*No kwargs or boolean flags.*

Produced by: canonical `<version>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code-block #code:eh-version-1>
<meta>
  <version | 1.0.0>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:eh-version-1>
<meta>
  <version | 1.0.0>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Semantic version. Other formats are equally valid as a free-form
string.*

<code #code:eh-version-2>
<meta version="draft-2" />
</code>

<minipage #mp:eh-version-2>
<meta version="draft-2" />
</minipage>

*Kwarg-form authoring lifts to the child-tag form at the gate.*
